149-3213-2549 exists when time is ignored, but the events fire in an order that breaks causality. The only interaction reaching 2549 is 3213->2549 in [46841,47040], which precedes 3213's contact with 4149 ([47041,47200]), which in turn precedes 7049<->4149 ([47201,47400]) and 4358<->7049 ([47601,47800]). Thus influence from 3027's single event ([46641,46840]) could not have propagated forward through this chain, and 2549 has no other in-neighbour in the window. Volume is low and both endpoints have degree 1, so popularity/volume confounds are ruled out.", "confidence": 0.5}, "raw_final_response": "## Reconstruction\n\n**Static connectivity exists** (step_04/step_05): 3027 \u2192 4358 \u2192 7049 \u2192 4149 \u2192 3213 \u2192 2549. So an order-ignoring path is present \u2014 but that alone is not sufficient.\n\n**Both endpoints are sparse, not \"popular\"** (step_02): 3027 and 2549 each have exactly 1 event in the window, so volume/popularity cannot explain the link.\n\n**Temporal ordering of the hops** (steps 06\u201316):\n| hop | time bucket |\n|---|---|\n| 3027 \u2192 4358 | [46641, 46840] |\n| 3213 \u2192 2549 (only event into 2549) | [46841, 47040] |\n| 4149 \u2194 3213 | [47041, 47200] |\n| 7049 \u2194 4149 | [47201, 47400] |\n| 4358 \u2194 7049 | [47601, 47800] |\n\nThe path's hops occur in essentially **reverse order** downstream of 4358: 4358 does not contact 7049 until ~47601\u201347800, yet 7049\u21944149 already happened at 47201\u201347400, 4149\u21943213 at 47041\u201347200, and the single delivery into 2549 (3213 \u2192 2549, step_16) at 46841\u201347040 \u2014 *before* 3213 had any contact with 4149. Node 2549 has no other in-edge in the window (step_05), and no further activity anywhere in the window for these nodes after 48160 (steps 06\u201311, apart from 4149's unrelated later events).\n\nSo no time-respecting, \u2264600-unit-gap chain from 3027 can reach 2549: the terminal hop fires before the upstream hops that would have carried the influence.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_9c9c8a9f\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [3027, 4358, 7049, 4149, 3213, 2549],\n  \"window\": [42400, 52000],\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"A static path 3027-4358-7049-4149-3213-2549 exists when time is ignored, but the events fire in an order that breaks causality. The only interaction reaching 2549 is 3213->2549 in [46841,47040], which precedes 3213's contact with 4149 ([47041,47200]), which in turn precedes 7049<->4149 ([47201,47400]) and 4358<->7049 ([47601,47800]). Thus influence from 3027's single event ([46641,46840]) could not have propagated forward through this chain, and 2549 has no other in-neighbour in the window. Volume is low and both endpoints have degree 1, so popularity/volume confounds are ruled out.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 34715, "total_output_tokens": 6606, "total_tokens": 41321, "total_latency_ms": 86193, "llm_calls": 7, "schema_repairs": 0, "tool_protocol_errors": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}